        "v": [
          "### Python code",
          "This module also assesses whether the paper's Python code could be run on its data, and — because `execute = TRUE` — **actually ran it**. We examined 4 Python code files.",
          "#### Run order",
          "No ordering signal (no data dependency, `source()`-equivalent, or numeric filename prefix) distinguishes the run order of these files. They may need to run in a specific order that could not be determined automatically — check this before running.",
          "\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(Order = 1:4, File = c(\"colab.py\", \"errors.py\", \n\"ok.py\", \"relative.py\"), \"Runs after\" = c(\"—\", \"—\", \"—\", \n\"—\"), Basis = c(\"none\", \"none\", \"none\", \"none\")), row.names = c(NA, \n-4L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 10, FALSE)\n```\n",
          "#### File paths",
          "Every data path in the code works in the repository as deposited.",
          "#### Execution",
          "**The Python code was run.** Each script ran in an isolated subprocess against a throwaway copy of the repository, in the run order above, with a 60-second per-script timeout. Of 4 scripts: 1 ran without error, 2 errored, 0 timed out, 1 could not run because one of its own dependencies is unavailable, 0 did not parse, and 0 are written for Python 2 and not run. Running against current package versions: a break can reflect version drift, which argues for pinning versions (e.g. in a `requirements.txt`).",
          "\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(File = c(\"colab.py\", \"errors.py\", \"ok.py\", \"relative.py\"\n), Outcome = c(\"dependency_unavailable\", \"errored\", \"ran_ok\", \n\"errored\"), Detail = c(\"dependency_unavailable\", \"RuntimeError\", \n\"\", \"ImportError\"), \"Time (s)\" = 0), row.names = c(NA, \n-4L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 15, FALSE)\n```\n",
          "**Dependency-unavailable errors**",
          "**1 script could not run because its own dependency is unavailable** — the package failed to `pip install`. This is an infrastructure limitation, not a defect in the paper's code, so it does **not** force the traffic light red.",
          "\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(File = \"colab.py\"), row.names = c(NA, -1L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 10, FALSE)\n```\n",
          "*Expand a row below to see the output each script produced.*",
          "::: {.callout-tip title=\"Output — colab.py (dependency_unavailable)\" collapse=\"true\"}\n\n**Messages / errors (stderr):**\n````\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<root>/colab.py\", line 1, in <module>\n    from google.colab import drive\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'google.colab'\n````\n\n:::\n",
          "::: {.callout-tip title=\"Output — errors.py (errored)\" collapse=\"true\"}\n\n**Messages / errors (stderr):**\n````\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<root>/errors.py\", line 6, in <module>\n    raise RuntimeError(\"deliberate failure for testing\")\nRuntimeError: deliberate failure for testing\n````\n\n:::\n",
